{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts","id":1520328,"title":"W20 Various Doubts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-10T15:30:04-07:00","id":1520328,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> W20 Various Doubts","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Lots of minor questions, these might be common knowledge but I am a bit ignorant on many details (also I might be just wrong):<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Can the Changing Breeds get the <b>Animal Magnetism</b> merit? There is a bit of overlap with the <b>Sex Appeal</b> merit that some breeds can get.</li> <li>How does the <b>Cat/Fox Magic </b>merit work? It states that &quot;<i>The character can use this talent to mimic Gifts and rites from any Changing Breed</i>&quot; but Foxes already &quot;<i>can easily learn the Gifts of other Changing Breeds as well, as long as they have a teacher for the Gift.</i>\u200b&quot; and I think Bastet can also copy from other breeds.</li> <li>Mechanically, what do you use <b>Appeareance </b>for besides first impressions? <b>Charisma </b>and <b>Manipulation </b>seem more impactful long term.</li> <li>Is there any limit to raising <b>Gnosis</b>, <b>Rage </b>and <b>Willpower </b>at character generation? It is a bit absurd to have a paragon of spiritual and mental fortitude as a starting character but seems perfectly valid by the rules.</li> <li>Hengeyokai refer to the <b>Wyrm </b>as the <b>Centipede</b>, and the <b>Weaver </b>as a <b>Spider</b>, which animal represents the <b>Wyld</b>?</li> <li>Can <b>Kuei-Jin</b> (or any other supernatural for tha matter) make use of Fetishes? By using a rite or power, I was reading the Nushi mechanics and it seems feasible, but I dont see it described anywhere. And it seems something that Mages could replicate, but no idea which spheres (Spirit + Prime perhaps?)</li> <li>Can Packmates teach rites to each other? The Core book says that the ones that teach must be Elders, but what stops two packamates from trading knowledge?</li> </ol>I might post further questions based on the answers.<br /> <br /> Thanks,\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a repost of my original thread, since the mods have not approved and it is in a limbo. I will delete the other thread when/if approved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-10-2024, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T16:17:31-07:00","id":1520333,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I tried to keep your contribution, I was able to copy from the original thread now<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there are some keys to when Appearance should be used versus the other Social attributes.<br /> <br /> One is whenever decisions are made based on visual information as opposed to the spoken word. Those are not necessarily limited to first impressions (in the sense it is the first time someone has met you). The silent person who stands up and stares at a rowdy crowd to be more respectful to those around them? Appearance + Intimidation works good for that roll. Even if the rowdy crowd has seen or even spoken to that person before and thus is not a &quot;first&quot; impression. Likewise if you want to conceal something on your body, but not have it be obvious - roll Appearance + Stealth. Dressing to fit in like you belong to a group and are not an outsider, roll Appearance + Streetwise or Appearance + Law (or whatever) depending on the social environment you'll be in. Want to sleep (or goof off) while on guard duty, but still appear like you are doing your job? Use Appearance + Alertness.<br /> <br /> Anything that might involve body language would be another. You can communicate a lot of basic things through body language even if you have an actual spoken conversation, which if transcribed would appear ordinary and innocuous. Anything from &quot;I don't like and you're not going to get anything from me&quot; to &quot;You are in danger if you stay because I am in danger as well, get out and call the police&quot; to &quot;I think you're hot, let's get out of here and have sex.&quot; You might want to extend that to other forms of non-verbal communication than just body language. What happens if you encounter someone who cannot speak the same language as you, but you need to communicate to them somehow? Appearance + Expression might be the best choice. Or you want to comfort someone in emotional pain or grief but think talking is inappropriate at this time? Appearance + Empathy could work. Someone taking others on a physical adventure and wants to show/teach them what kind of gear they need to take with them and how to pack it and carry it on themselves? They may want to outfit themselves first and display it to others visually because that is more effective than talking about it abstractly - roll Appearance + Survival.<br /> <br /> Anytime you want to showcase physical perfection or elegance. A ballerina wanting to appear graceful in a performance might not be rolling Dexterity + Performance, but Appearance + Performance instead. Or you might need to roll both for looking great while performing a particularly difficult stunt. A gymnast doing a particularly difficult stunt may need to roll Dexterity first to simply do it, but then also roll Appearance so she looks graceful and elegant while doing it in order to get that 10 out of 10. Similarly a gunfighter may need Dexterity + Firearms to actually hit a target, but if he wants to do an impressive looking quick draw or other gunslinging stunts use Appearance + Firearms. Want to impress the rubes that your occult ceremony is spectacular? Select the right clothing, aesthetics of your ritual area, and your physical performance of the rites by rolling Appearance + Occult.<br /> <br /> There may also be times when Appearance is an attribute used on people or objects other than yourself. If you can make yourself look good, then you can use your aesthetic skills to make someone else look good. Want to turn the ugly duckling wallflower into a stunning Cinderella? Use Appearance + Etiquette. A cosmetologist putting makeup on a customer (or a mortuary worker putting make up a dead person to make them presentable for the wake)? Appearance + Crafts.<br /> <br /> Now in some of these cases, an ST or player may want to achieve the same goal, but not want to use Appearance but another attribute. And I think that would be fine too. Very often there are multiple ways of accomplishing the same thing, and I'll allow players to suggest different trait combinations than the ones I originally ask for. But Appearance can definitely be used more often in the game than just &quot;I want to look good in front of other people and have them find me attractive.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Adding Black Fox's comments. 08-12-2023, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T16:43:22-07:00","id":1520336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts#post1520328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Changing Breeds get the <b>Animal Magnetism</b> merit? There is a bit of overlap with the <b>Sex Appeal</b> merit that some breeds can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally the core book Merits are open to the other Changers. However all Merits and Flaws are meant to be up to ST discretion. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does the <b>Cat/Fox Magic </b>merit work? </div> </div> </div>It lets you buy Numina Paths from books like Sorcerer. However, so it can be useful for people that don't buy non-WtA supplements, you can use Gifts and Rites to mechanically represent this instead (the same way the sample supernatural antagonists in the core book use Gifts instead of the powers of their supernatural type)<br /> .<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, what do you use <b>Appeareance </b>for besides first impressions? <b>Charisma </b>and <b>Manipulation </b>seem more impactful long term. </div> </div> </div>RAW Appearance is a dump stat. You can push a bit via using ST discretion, but if you want Appearance to be useful outside of a few Gifts, you're going to get into house rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any limit to raising <b>Gnosis</b>, <b>Rage </b>and <b>Willpower </b>at character generation? It is a bit absurd to have a paragon of spiritual and mental fortitude as a starting character but seems perfectly valid by the rules. </div> </div> </div>There's no mechanical limits besides your limited Freebie points and them all capping at 10. Depending on your starting splats, you are either spending the vast majority of your points to do this, or even not even able to get to 10s in them.<br /> <br /> Raising Rage at normal char-gen is also a horrible idea, even if you buy up Gnosis and Willpower to avoid the worst possible outcomes. Starting Garou don't have the tools of more experienced characters to help resist Frenzies.<br /> <br /> As usual, this is why the games rely on people to run them: it's the ST's role to look at a character and decide if they're appropriate for the specific instance of the game about to be played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hengeyokai refer to the <b>Wyrm </b>as the <b>Centipede</b>, and the <b>Weaver </b>as a <b>Spider</b>, which animal represents the <b>Wyld</b>? </div> </div> </div>AFAIK there isn't one. The Wyld is... somewhat opposed to such labels. The original book uses the term &quot;goblin&quot; to describe the Wyld distorted Yang spirits of the Asian Umbra, though I don't think they specified which word for such monsters in an actual Asian language they were going with that might make it easier to apply an guess on what a local term for the Wyld would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can <b>Kuei-Jin</b> (or any other supernatural for tha matter) make use of Fetishes? By using a rite or power, I was reading the Nushi mechanics and it seems feasible, but I dont see it described anywhere. And it seems something that Mages could replicate, but no idea which spheres (Spirit + Prime perhaps?) </div> </div> </div>A lot of supernaturals can potentially learn to use Fetishe, though how varies considerably. Mages just use Willpower instead of Gnosis to attune and activate them. They only need Spirit to make them. Though most Spirit mages would caution against using a Fetish without Spirit, since that's a great way to piss off your Wonder and have no idea how to placate it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Packmates teach rites to each other? The Core book says that the ones that teach must be Elders, but what stops two packamates from trading knowledge? </div> </div> </div>The tradition is that you seek such things from high ranking Garou as it relates the tacit approval of your reasons to learn the Rite. There's no mechanical reason to stop packmates from teaching each other Rites, though the disrespect for tradition could result in a mild Renown penalty and/or a denial of the normal Renown for learning rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T16:54:41-07:00","id":1520339,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Thanks for the answers, some doubts I have on the points you raised..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520336#post1520336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RAW Appearance is a dump stat. You can push a bit via using ST discretion, but if you want Appearance to be useful outside of a few Gifts, you're going to get into house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there truly no mechanical use for it? I see of course a roleplaying difference in someone with a value 1 and somebody with 5 arriving at a party or a business meeting, but I was looking for any mechanical usage (besides first impressions).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520336#post1520336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of supernaturals can potentially learn to use Fetishe, though how varies considerably. <b>Mages just use Willpower instead of Gnosis to attune and activate them. They only need Spirit to make them. </b>Though most Spirit mages would caution against using a Fetish without Spirit, since that's a great way to piss off your Wonder and have no idea how to placate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this stated? And does a mage created Fetish (Spirit 4, right?) work for Fera/Garou normally?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520336#post1520336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> The tradition is that you seek such things from high ranking Garou as it relates the tacit approval of your reasons to learn the Rite. There's no mechanical reason to stop packmates from teaching each other Rites, though the disrespect for tradition could result in a mild Renown penalty and/or a denial of the normal Renown for learning rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there any leeway for situations where there are no Elders around? Or what happens if your elders get out of the picture (death, gone, or your pack is the one that moved places). I ask mainly if there are any rulings for this, or if it was described in any supplement/novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T17:16:09-07:00","id":1520341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts#post1520328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Lots of minor questions, these might be common knowledge but I am a bit ignorant on many details (also I might be just wrong):<br /> Can the Changing Breeds get the <b>Animal Magnetism</b> merit? There is a bit of overlap with the <b>Sex Appeal</b> merit that some breeds can get.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd probably less cringe if you called it Sex Appeal all around, frankly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mechanically, what do you use <b>Appeareance </b>for besides first impressions? <b>Charisma </b>and <b>Manipulation </b>seem more impactful long term. </div> </div> </div>Exalted 3rd edition has some suggestions on that front, as it's just used when Charisma or Manipulation might be, but when you're using your presence and looks instead of doing much talking. It's also used for leading mass combat from the front (something you're more likely to see in Werewolf or Changeling than most other WoD games), communicating via gesture, or a passive effect that messes with the dispositions of characters with lower Wits. It's also used for some Gifts, though this is less common.<br /> <br /> In the original 1e versions of WoD games, the gating effect of first impressions was also more sensible - instead of limiting an entire social dice pool, it limited the final number of successes that applied to characters who didn't know you. So in Werewolf, what Appearance for is for getting your foot in the door when your Renown isn't high enough or people simply just don't know you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any limit to raising <b>Gnosis</b>, <b>Rage </b>and <b>Willpower </b>at character generation? It is a bit absurd to have a paragon of spiritual and mental fortitude as a starting character but seems perfectly valid by the rules. </div> </div> </div>Sometimes you've just lived a life that put you there. That's part of why lupus start with Gnosis 5, and why werebears start with Willpower 6. Just think of it as the character type that might not be quite as gifted in terms of expertise, but who has heart.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a possibility for using some merits to blunt the impact of high Rage. Calm Heart places your difficulty 2 higher; I can't recall off hand if there are any other, but definitely do not get Mars Midsky if you have high Rage...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hengeyokai refer to the <b>Wyrm </b>as the <b>Centipede</b>, and the <b>Weaver </b>as a <b>Spider</b>, which animal represents the <b>Wyld</b>? </div> </div> </div>Some Mages in Dragons of the East framed the Metaphysical Trinity and Triat as a tiger for Wyld, phoenix for Weaver, and dragon for the Wyrm, but this is counter to how those animals are typically presented in Sino-xenic cultures, which tend to go for four legendary beasts, with the tiger representing a rather more Weaver-ish bent because of associations with the xing of metal and Dragon Wyld-ish because of being used to represent the xing of wood.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T17:23:03-07:00","id":1520343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520339#post1520339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Thanks for the answers, some doubts I have on the points you raised..<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there truly no mechanical use for it? I see of course a roleplaying difference in someone with a value 1 and somebody with 5 arriving at a party or a business meeting, but I was looking for any mechanical usage (besides first impressions).</div> </div> </div> </div>The pairings of Attributes and Abilities in Storyteller games is fairly open-ended; anything could theoretically be paired with anything else, under a particular set of circumstances. Strength + Empathy is unlikely, but could come up; Appearance is likely to come up a lot more often simply by virtue of it being all about grabbing attention from anyone it can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this stated? And does a mage created Fetish (Spirit 4, right?) work for Fera/Garou normally? </div> </div> </div>In Mage, and maybe. It might be cursed from being forced into existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any leeway for situations where there are no Elders around? Or what happens if your elders get out of the picture (death, gone, or your pack is the one that moved places). I ask mainly if there are any rulings for this, or if it was described in any supplement/novel. </div> </div> </div>Ancestor-spirits could also potentially teach them, I believe, so long as they knew them in life, which is kind of an arbitrary measure; to more fully define this, approach your ST about having the Ancestor Ally merit and having your ancestor-spirit be your post-death Obi Wan bought as Mentor. Also, don't go looking for novels for game information in the WoD, because the novels frequently don;'t follow them. I believe the term is &quot;canon on crack&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T17:30:34-07:00","id":1520344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520339#post1520339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there truly no mechanical use for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the default rolls in Seduction actions. A few of the sample social actions offer the option of using Appearance instead of the usual Attribute if the ST rules it appropriate.<br /> <br /> Appearance has been a contentious trait because of this for over 30 years (and not just for WtA). Like... I'm not sure what you want me to say? The rules for Appearance in the classic WoD editions are bad. Your first impression wasn't faulty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this stated? And does a mage created Fetish (Spirit 4, right?) work for Fera/Garou normally? </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly sure Fetish has been a Spirit 4 effect since Mage 1e.<br /> <br /> In general, yes, mage made Fetishes aren't fundamentally different from ones made with Fera Rites. However, many mages bind spirits against the spirits' will, and such Fetishes might choose to not function or function oddly for Fera and demand their freedom instead. Given how little mages are trusted, plenty of the Shiters might assume any mage crafted Fetish should be destroyed to free the spirit free on general principle too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any leeway for situations where there are no Elders around? Or what happens if your elders get out of the picture (death, gone, or your pack is the one that moved places). I ask mainly if there are any rulings for this, or if it was described in any supplement/novel. </div> </div> </div>Did I not just post some leeway?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T19:00:40-07:00","id":1520350,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Another question, can Fera buy the <b>Zodiacal </b>and<b> Planetary Aspects </b>merits/flaws?<br /> <br /> And the damage chart of Ranged weapons has a set value, is it automatic damage (once it hits) or it is damage dice that you roll? (For example a Revolver says Damage 4, it is 4 dice or 4 points of damage?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-10-2023, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T19:16:34-07:00","id":1520351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520350#post1520350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> Another question, can Fera buy the <b>Zodiacal </b>and<b> Planetary Aspects </b>merits/flaws?<br /> <br /> And the damage chart of Ranged weapons has a set value, is it automatic damage (once it hits) or it is damage dice that you roll? (For example a Revolver says Damage 4, it is 4 dice or 4 points of damage?)</div> </div> </div> </div>In order, probably, and the damage is given in dice, which you add to your net attack successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T01:19:27-07:00","id":1520361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520339#post1520339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Where is this stated? And does a mage created Fetish (Spirit 4, right?) work for Fera/Garou normally?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> it is referenced in Mage's corebooks, IIRC alongside wonders and other artifacts.<br /> In the same way, vampire sorcerers with the spiritual thaumaturgy path can create fetishes (although they are nerfed in V20) and used blood points to activate them.<br /> <br /> And as far as I know, all fetishes, regardless of their creation are fetishes for everyone, so a tremere could use a stolen garou's fetish as much as a garou could use a stolen mage's fetish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520339#post1520339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there any leeway for situations where there are no Elders around? Or what happens if your elders get out of the picture (death, gone, or your pack is the one that moved places). I ask mainly if there are any rulings for this, or if it was described in any supplement/novel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, nothing stop any garou from teaching a rite to anyone. It's juste against custom and might be seen as a mockery of traditio if done without a good reason.<br /> <br /> As for the ruling, since there never was rules for player teaching other player characters (outside of wraith 20th), I would advise to simply do as you would with an elder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T01:56:11-07:00","id":1520363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520361#post1520361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as far as I know, all fetishes, regardless of their creation are fetishes for everyone, so a tremere could use a stolen garou's fetish as much as a garou could use a stolen mage's fetish.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fetishes don't work if they are not treated correctly and quite a few of them need a gnosis roll to activate. While I can see mages using Arete to activate a Fetish, I don't really see how a vampire could activate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T02:01:53-07:00","id":1520364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520343#post1520343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The pairings of Attributes and Abilities in Storyteller games is fairly open-ended; anything could theoretically be paired with anything else, under a particular set of circumstances. Strength + Empathy is unlikely, but could come up; Appearance is likely to come up a lot more often simply by virtue of it being all about grabbing attention from anyone it can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually had a Strength + Empathy pop up recently. Can't remember what it was but it made sense at the time. The ideas in other systems about using Appearance towards impressing others, leading others or even getting people to do things without words has helped make it work better than the official &quot;First Impressions&quot; take.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T02:03:00-07:00","id":1520365,"title":"","content":"While it's not a default power of the Spiritus Discipline, it's a pretty obvious combo to make. There are spirit focused Paths of Thaumaturgy/etc. that allow Fetish use and making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T05:19:36-07:00","id":1520376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520363#post1520363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetishes don't work if they are not treated correctly and quite a few of them need a gnosis roll to activate. While I can see mages using Arete to activate a Fetish, I don't really see how a vampire could activate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Spiritual Thaumaturgy rules, any vampire with at least 4 points in the path rating (the level required to force a spirit into a fetish) can activate a fetish by paying a blood point as he would for any use of blood magic.<br /> <br /> As for fetish not working if the spirit isn't well treated, since it's nowhere to be found in either vtm or mta, this sound like a wta thing that was never translated to other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T05:30:45-07:00","id":1520377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520363#post1520363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fetishes don't work if they are not treated correctly and quite a few of them need a gnosis roll to activate. While I can see mages using Arete to activate a Fetish, I don't really see how a vampire could activate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC you can bully Fetish Spirits to work with Spirit Thauma. An Ahrimane or Lhiannan might be able to convince a Fetish Spirit by using their Disciplines, but I don't think it's an explicit power. Some necromancers can at least craft Fetish-like objects with bound Wraiths, but I don't think that power extends to proper Spirits. All other Vampires are probably out of luck unless they have something (high Auspex?) to threaten the Spirit into action.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should read the other answers before making redundant posts. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-11-2023, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T06:05:27-07:00","id":1520379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520365#post1520365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's not a default power of the Spiritus Discipline, it's a pretty obvious combo to make. There are spirit focused Paths of Thaumaturgy/etc. that allow Fetish use and making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiritus does count as rather exotic and the provenance of a female only exotic bloodline that disappeared for the better part of History, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T08:57:44-07:00","id":1520389,"title":"","content":"Sure, though Thaum having a way to do it means most Tremere would be able to research that it's a thing and that it's possible even if vampires that know how are rare.<br /> <br /> I was just pointing out how vampires could theoretically use a Fetish, not that it would be common for them to do so (esp. with how little they get to play in the Umbra sandbox).<br /> <br /> It's definitely in stark contrast to anything with a Gnosis rating that can inherently attune and use Fetishes, or mages that can exert their will over a Fetish using the magic binding the spirit to compel activation even if most mages don't necessarily realize they don't actually need Spirit to do that. But it is possible for vampires to learn how to do with canon rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T09:36:06-07:00","id":1520395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520389#post1520389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, though Thaum having a way to do it means most Tremere would be able to research that it's a thing and that it's possible even if vampires that know how are rare.<br /> <br /> I was just pointing out how vampires could theoretically use a Fetish, not that it would be common for them to do so (esp. with how little they get to play in the Umbra sandbox).<br /> <br /> It's definitely in stark contrast to anything with a Gnosis rating that can inherently attune and use Fetishes, or <b>mages that can exert their will over a Fetish using the magic binding the spirit to compel activation even if most mages don't necessarily realize they don't actually need Spirit to do that.</b> But it is possible for vampires to learn how to do with canon rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be an Arete roll, or usage of other Spheres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T11:50:26-07:00","id":1520401,"title":"","content":"M20, p 562:<br /> <br /> &quot;A Fetish channels the power of a spirit within that item. To use one, the character asks the spirit to unleash its powers. Storywise, this typically demands a decent relationship with the spirit in question; game-wise, the Storyteller might have the player make a Willpower roll (difficulty 7) against the spirit\u2019s Gnosis Trait. A successful roll employs that Gnosis as the dice pool for the Fetish\u2019s effects, so a Gnosis 5 Fetish would have a five-die pool.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bThe the mechanics are clearly a bit different (in Mage, designing a Fetish works like any other Wonder, hence the need to roll its Gnosis to see how well the effect goes off), but to activate a Fetish, a mage just needs to win the Willpower vs Gnosis contested roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T16:50:13-07:00","id":1520480,"title":"","content":"Another question:<br /> <br /> The <b>Natural Linguist</b> Merit adds &quot;three dice to any dice pool involving written or spoken language\u200b&quot;, does this mean that this is a blank +3 dice to each social written or verbal interaction?<br /> <br /> <br /> Your thoughts please <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>,, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:12:55-07:00","id":1520483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520480#post1520480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question:<br /> <br /> The <b>Natural Linguist</b> Merit adds &quot;three dice to any dice pool involving written or spoken language\u200b&quot;, does this mean that this is a blank +3 dice to each social written or verbal interaction?<br /> <br /> <br /> Your thoughts please <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>,, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Well by my read this applies to the use of the linguistics skill. Not to every use of spoken or written word. So if you wanted to translate a text from Sumerian this is what you would use. It wouldn't allow you to gain bonus dice on a letter that would persuade your Mentor to move out of his cave and come down to your Caern in its hour of need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:18:04-07:00","id":1520485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520480#post1520480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Natural Linguist</b> Merit adds &quot;three dice to any dice pool involving written or spoken language\u200b&quot;, does this mean that this is a blank +3 dice to each social written or verbal interaction?[/USER]</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is, the Merit is grossly overpowered. The sentence on adding three dice to any roll involving language comes from the original description of this Merit back in 1e when Linguistics was an actual Knowledge ability. If I was the ST, I would have limited those three extra dice to rolls that actually involved the Linguistics ability, not every single time the character is speaking and makes a roll. Maybe not strictly limited to Linguistics because that was almost never used in games (and to be fair, the merit itself does not say Linguistics dice pool). But it would have to be a roll where the <i>technicalities</i> of language and grammar come into play.<br /> <br /> Although the old Linguistics ability was mainly about knowing extra languages, it did provide things like identifying accents and reading lips. And it had example Specialties like Curse Words, Technical, Diplomatic, Political. So I think the intention for the ability was to allow it to be used whenever understanding meaning is difficult, and getting the right translation is critical. So such rolls might come up when translating an archaic version of the language, a difficult dialect or sister language, choosing the correct terms when writing treaties, trying to determine the most likely meaning of a text that has lacuna, detecting a forgery, or knowing that in Latin Jehovah is spelled with an &quot;I&quot; when trying to figure out a puzzle or riddle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WskWZfFpWNI\" data-code=\"WskWZfFpWNI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/WskWZfFpWNI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> These types of things will need to be determined by some other Ability since Linguistics no longer exists. So an ST might call for an Academics, Enigmas, Law, Occult, etc. roll instead.<br /> <br /> That's how I would adjudicate it initially, but am open to others' opinions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-12-2023, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T17:26:42-07:00","id":1520487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520485#post1520485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These types of things will need to be determined by some other Ability since Linguistics no longer exists. So an ST might call for an Academics, Enigmas, Law, Occult, etc. roll instead.<br /> <br /> That's how I would adjudicate it initially, but am open to others' opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe Linguistics could still be an optional focus skill for playing characters just like Jackson. A highly specialised skills for uncovering clues and ancient languages without necessarily speaking them fluently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:10:35-07:00","id":1520490,"title":"","content":"I ask because the M20 equivalent does grant 3 dice <i>&quot;when making rolls based upon clear communications, typically ones employing <b>Art, Expression, Etiquette, Leadership</b>, and other traits that involve 'speaking their language' to impress someone else.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:11:48-07:00","id":1520491,"title":"","content":"Rmemeber that I titled the thread with W20. There is no linguistics skill, just Language merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:16:30-07:00","id":1520492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520491#post1520491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rmemeber that I titled the thread with W20. There is no linguistics skill, just Language merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because there is not a skill on the default sheet, doesn't meant that optional skills are not available for the characters that need them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T18:57:33-07:00","id":1520496,"title":"","content":"As well, it's important that since the 20th books are Anniversary Editions, there's a lot of carry over from older editions in them that didn't necessarily get updated when things were changed in other parts of the books.<br /> <br /> I would concur with previous posters: The merit's bonus dice should apply to rolls that are either about interpreting/recognizing linguistic details, or modifying your speech to adapt to circumstances; not a flat +3 to everything that uses a language in speech or text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T05:44:18-07:00","id":1520586,"title":"","content":"I'm joining the chorus at this point, but I agree with the others: it's probably a hold-over from the Linguistics Skill. I would go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>' interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:03:52-07:00","id":1520664,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all for the answers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I do agree that a blank +3 is insanely strong, but the wording is extremely vague. At least M20 equivalent had some more detailed examples on how and when it works.<br /> <br /> I actually think that making it a one dot Merit, whose only effect is doubling the number of language that the Language merit grants would be a simpler solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:10:43-07:00","id":1520665,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of copy-paste issues in W20 where bits are not working consistently page to page. For instance it has references to BOTH the multiple action systems in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T10:07:15-07:00","id":1520684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1520664#post1520664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that making it a one dot Merit, whose only effect is doubling the number of language that the Language merit grants would be a simpler solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simpler isn't always better though. Sure, more languages for your buck is definitely simpler, but it has knock on effects on how to adjudicate what counts as a language, or how to make someone that's good with all the variations of a language. The whole point of Merits (and why they're generally treated as semi-optional in the WoD books), is to add granularity to the game.<br /> <br /> If you just reduce Natural Linguist to extra language, then it's at best a point trap: if you intend on getting more than one Language Merit, you should buy Natural Linguist first. At that point you might as well not even have it as a separate Merit and just roll it into a function of the Language Merit itself where after being bi- or trilingual, future Language Merits start getting you more languages so people don't don't waste a bunch of points if they missed that Natural Linguist exists.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there's nothing for denoting that your character is someone that's good at spotting accents, dialects, code-switching, regional slang and colloquialisms, archaic/academic/dead language uses, and so on. Something that I think social media has somewhat hidden in pop culture, is just how much written word vs spoken word can be radically different when it comes to mutual understanding. As well, and this can be pretty important for something like the WoD where you have beings that were around centuries ago, languages change, drastically, over time. An Ancestor spirit that naturally speaks English,but English from a thousand years ago, might as well mean needing to find someone with Spirit Speech to translate instead of trying to communicate with them via modern English. <br /> <br /> So, something that Natural Linguist makes much, much, simpler is reducing the number of instances of the Language Merit you &quot;need&quot; to include the sheer variety within linguistics. However much it's a massive abstraction still, forcing someone to buy modern English, Middle English, and Old English to speak all of English isn't really &quot;fun.&quot; Unless your game involves a lot of time travel or something, it just feels penalizing to do that, but it would feel very weird to have someone that only knows modern English to be able freely communicate with older versions of the language without magic because... they are different languages. To me, this is the much more important function because it's what someone play an linguist style characters wants to be able to do: they want to be able to navigate all these subtle changes that build up over time; not rack up a giant list of highly specific languages.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T14:46:28-07:00","id":1520708,"title":"","content":"To be fair, language related abilities have always been something that RPGs struggled with doing the split between game convenience and realism. The ST system isn't alone with that, and they tried quite a few things throughout editions and game lines. The Natural Linguist Merit suffers a bit from trying to cover too many things at once; being able to easily pick up new languages and being proficient in using rhetoric efficiently are two different skill-sets and should be two different Merits imo.<br /> <br /> The 'fair' option would be to have separate Abilities for each language, a learning Merit that reduces XP cost, and a proficiency Merit that gives bonus dice. That's an incredible XP sink if you charge full cost, and there are people who grow up with multiple languages natively. Plus, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> mentioned, the application for dead languages is limited. Languages as Merit seems a good compromise, but then you're less flexible with what you can do with Merits mechanically. I personally still like to cover general proficiency with the Linguistics Ability and treat known languages as something that goes as note on the sheet, independently from dotted stats. There's also the option to cover dead languages with the Academics ability, for languages like Latin, Ancient Greek, Sanskrit, and Middle [European language].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T16:03:29-07:00","id":1521080,"title":"","content":"Another couple of questions:<br /> <br /> Did the Changing Breed book get an errata?<br /> I find that the gift list and the Breed/Auspice-Equivalent descriptions do not match. For example Kitsune Doshi says: <b>Blessing the Blade, Sense Magic, Spirit Speech</b>; but the gift list \u200bis<b> Blessing the Blade</b>, <b>Breath of Yu-Chiang</b>, <b>Sense Wyrm</b>, <b>Shroud</b>; same happens with several other gift lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T16:27:46-07:00","id":1521082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1521080#post1521080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another couple of questions:<br /> <br /> Did the Changing Breed book get an errata?<br /> I find that the gift list and the Breed/Auspice-Equivalent descriptions do not match. For example Kitsune Doshi says: <b>Blessing the Blade, Sense Magic, Spirit Speech</b>; but the gift list \u200bis<b> Blessing the Blade</b>, <b>Breath of Yu-Chiang</b>, <b>Sense Wyrm</b>, <b>Shroud</b>; same happens with several other gift lists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regrettably, you can count on most X20 stuff never getting errata. The last chance to change material was about a decade ago during the pre-release editing passes; after that, I doubt that they have the resources or could get the approval to change anything.<br /> <br /> However, this doesn't seem to be a big error. Just a copy-paste of material from Hengeyokai (additional Gifts were added in Player's Guide to the Changing Breed, from Revised). Any level one Gift in a category is generally okay for a starting character, even if the chargen section doesn't mention it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T17:12:12-07:00","id":1521085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520328-w20-various-doubts?p=1521082#post1521082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regrettably, you can count on most X20 stuff never getting errata. The last chance to change material was about a decade ago during the pre-release editing passes; after that, I doubt that they have the resources or could get the approval to change anything.<br /> <br /> However, this doesn't seem to be a big error. Just a copy-paste of material from Hengeyokai (additional Gifts were added in Player's Guide to the Changing Breed, from Revised). Any level one Gift in a category is generally okay for a starting character, even if the chargen section doesn't mention it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, but then which one is the valid list? The ones on the Breed/Path/Auspice description or the detailed list in the Gifts sections?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T19:15:20-07:00","id":1521093,"title":"","content":"Gift lists are ever-expanding, so it's not really reasonable to say &quot;well, this list in the chargen sections says these, so they're your only choices&quot;. So, in general, the Gift list, not the chargen section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}